3. Build a Coding Agent Pipeline
HyperCode’s coding flow should be a repeatable pipeline rather than one giant autonomous agent.

Suggested agent crew
Agent	Job	Can modify code?
Intent Agent	Turns messy ideas into clear goals	No
Project Mapper	Understands repository structure	No
Architect Agent	Designs implementation options	No
Builder Agent	Writes code in a temporary branch	Yes
Test Agent	Runs tests and creates failure reports	No
Security Agent	Checks secrets, permissions, dependencies, injection risks	No
Reviewer Agent	Reviews the diff against the goal	No
Documentation Agent	Updates README, changelog, and handover notes	Yes
Release Agent	Merges, deploys, and tags releases	Only with approval
Learning Agent	Converts the session into reusable knowledge	Yes
The key design principle is separation of duties. The same agent that writes code should not be the only agent allowed to approve, test, and release that code.

