12. Add a Secure Execution Plane
Generated code must run in a disposable environment.

Minimum controls
Rootless containers.

Read-only base filesystem.

CPU and memory limits.

Network disabled by default.

No host Docker socket.

Temporary workspace only.

Secret injection only when explicitly approved.

Command allowlists for sensitive operations.

Automatic cleanup after every run.

Full stdout, stderr, and exit-code capture.

A generated command such as rm -rf, a dependency install script, or a Docker socket request should trigger a policy check before execution.

