Integrating AGUI for real-time agent streams

Bro — use AG-UI as HyperCode’s streaming contract between FastAPI agents and the HyperCode dashboard. It turns invisible agent work into live, structured events: planning, tool calls, code changes, test outcomes, approvals, and errors.

Why It Matters
Your platform has many containers and specialist agents, so plain logs will become noisy fast. AG-UI gives every run a consistent lifecycle, including RUN_STARTED, step events, streamed text, tool-call events, state snapshots, and a clear finished or error outcome.

For HyperCode, this means Mission Control can show:

Now: what the agent is doing.

Next: the upcoming planned step.

Evidence: tool results, changed files, tests, and logs.

Decision: an approval card when a risky action needs Bro.

Recovery: error, retry, rollback, or escalation status.

Recommended Shape
Keep AG-UI at the edge of the orchestration layer. Your internal agents can keep their existing implementation style; an adapter translates their lifecycle and tool telemetry into AG-UI events.

text
Dashboard / Agents IDE
        │
        │ POST /api/agui/runs
        ▼
HyperCode AG-UI Gateway (FastAPI)
        │
        ├── validates request + identity
        ├── creates run_id + trace_id
        ├── streams AG-UI SSE events
        ▼
Crew Orchestrator
        │
        ├── Planner Agent
        ├── Builder Agent
        ├── Test Agent
        ├── Security Agent
        └── Healer Agent
                │
                ▼
Tools / MCP / Docker / GitHub / Tests
AG-UI servers accept a run request and emit lifecycle, message, and tool-call events; the usual transport is Server-Sent Events (SSE).

Event Contract
Start small. These events will cover most HyperCode runs:

HyperCode moment	AG-UI event
User starts a task	RUN_STARTED
Planner creates a plan	STEP_STARTED, custom hypercode.plan.created
Agent writes explanation	TEXT_MESSAGE_START, TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT, TEXT_MESSAGE_END
Agent begins a tool action	TOOL_CALL_START
Tool arguments stream	TOOL_CALL_ARGS
Tool invocation is ready	TOOL_CALL_END
Docker/test/GitHub action returns	TOOL_CALL_RESULT
Agent changes branch/files	custom hypercode.diff.ready
Tests begin and finish	custom hypercode.test.started / hypercode.test.finished
Human decision is needed	custom hypercode.approval.required
Successful job completion	RUN_FINISHED
Failure or policy block	RUN_ERROR
Tool calls conventionally stream as a start event, one or more arguments events, and an end event; a run should end with either RUN_FINISHED or RUN_ERROR.

