How to implement the AGUI adapter for FastAPI agents

Bro — build the adapter as a thin translation layer. It should convert your existing FastAPI agent/orchestrator events into AG-UI SSE events, without forcing a rewrite of every HyperCode agent.

AG-UI is specifically designed for an agent server to emit lifecycle, text, tool-call, state, and error events to a frontend over a streaming response.

Why This Shape
HyperCode already has multiple services and agents. A separate adapter means:

Existing agents keep working.

The dashboard gets one standard real-time stream.

You can add agents gradually.

Security, redaction, tracing, and approval checks live in one place.

Do not expose every container directly to the browser. Put one authenticated FastAPI gateway in front of the orchestrator.

