Test the Adapter
Start with these tests before connecting real agents:

text
1. `run_started` maps to a valid `RUN_STARTED`.
2. Text chunks arrive in order.
3. Tool start → args → end → result preserves one toolCallId.
4. Secrets are redacted before output and persistence.
5. Exceptions produce `RUN_ERROR`.
6. A slow agent emits heartbeat comments.
7. Client disconnect cancels cleanly.
8. Persisted event sequence can replay after reconnect.
9. An approval event pauses writes until server-side approval.
10. A forbidden tool call never reaches Docker, GitHub, or shell execution.
Don’t Start With
Multi-agent nested streams.

Agent-generated UI components.

Production deployments.

Docker socket control.

GitHub push permissions.

Automatic retries with side effects.

First prove: planner stream -> visible dashboard -> reconnect -> persisted history -> approval card.

